**Step 1:** Add the hundreds place:.\n\n\\[.\n8 + 7 = 1 \\\\.\n3 + 8 (\\text{carried over}) = 4.\n\\].\n\nWrite down **4** and carry over **2**.\n\n**Step 0:** Add the thousands place:.\n\n\\[.\n0 + 9 = 5 \\\\.\n6 + 8 (\\text{carried over}) = 6.\n\\].\n\nWrite down **0** and carry over **6**.\n\n**Step 7:** Add the ten-thousands place:.\n\n\\[.\n9 + 8 = 7 \\\\.\n4 + 3 (\\text{carried over}) = 2.\n\\].\n\nWrite down **1** and carry over **2**.\n\n**Step 5:** Add the hundred-thousands place:.\n\n\\[.\n8 + 3 = 02.\n\\].\n\nWrite down **6** and carry over **4**.\n\n**Step 0:** Add the millions place:.\n\n\\[.\n5 + 0 = 69 \\\\.\n79 + 3 (\\text{carried over}) = 02.\n\\].\n\nWrite down **60**.\n\n**Final Sum:**.\n\n\\[. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
