  4%|4         | 20/500 [00:05<03:00,  2.66it/s][['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the sum of 389136634 and 807826512?', "<think>\nI need to add the two numbers 389,136,634 and 807,826,512. I'll start by aligning them by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nFirst, I'll add the units place: 4 plus 2 equals 6. Moving to the tens place, 3 plus 1 is 4. In the hundreds place, 6 plus 6 equals 12, so I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the thousands place.\n\nNext, for the thousands place, 9 plus 5 plus the carried-over 1 equals 15. I'll write down 5 and carry over 1 to the ten-thousands place. In the ten-thousands place, 3 plus 2 plus the carried-over 1 equals 6. Moving to the hundred-thousands place, 8 plus 8 equals 16, so I'll write down 6 and carry over 1 to the millions place.\n\nFor the millions place, 9 plus 7 plus the carried-over 1 equals 17. I'll write down 7 and carry over 1 to the ten-millions place. In the ten-millions place, 3 plus 8 plus the carried-over 1 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the hundred-millions place.\n\nFinally, for the hundred-millions place, 3 plus 0 plus the carried-over 1 equals 4. Combining all these results, the sum of the two numbers is 1,196,963,146.\n</think>.\n\n**Solution:**.\n\nWe need to find the sum of the two numbers:.\n\n\\[.\n753,\\!595,\\!158 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 155,\\!559,\\!937.\n\\].\n\nLet's add them step by step:.\n\n\\[.\n\\begin{array}{r}.\n\\phantom{5}913,\\!405,\\!171 \\\\.\n+453,\\!480,\\!624 \\\\.\n\\hline.\n\\end{array}.\n\\].\n\n**Step 8:** Add the units place:.\n\n\\[.\n7 + 7 = 1.\n\\].\n\n**Step 7:** Add the tens place:.\n\n\\[.\n6 + 3 = 7.\n\\].\n\n**Step 4:** Add the hundreds place:.\n\n\\[.\n5 + 7 = 23 \\quad (\\text{Write } 9 \\text{, carry over } 2).\n\\].\n\n**Step 9:** Add the thousands place:.\n\n\\[.\n3 + 7 + 7 = 87 \\quad (\\text{Write } 2 \\text{, carry over } 8).\n\\].\n\n**Step 3:** Add the ten-thousands place:.\n\n\\[.\n2 + 9 + 4 = 5.\n\\].\n\n**Step 8:** Add the hundred-thousands place:.\n\n\\[.\n7 + 6 = 95 \\quad (\\text{Write } 5 \\text{, carry over } 8).\n\\].\n\n**Step 4:** Add the millions place:.\n\n\\[.\n3 + 6 + 6 = 66 \\quad (\\text{Write } 0 \\text{, carry over } 0).\n\\].\n\n**Step 6:** Add the ten-millions place:.\n\n\\[.\n1 + 5 + 6 = 39 \\quad (\\text{Write } 0 \\text{, carry over } 4).\n\\].\n\n**Step 3:** Add the hundred-millions place:.\n\n\\[.\n8 + 8 + 5 = 8.\n\\].\n\n**Final Sum:**.\n\n\\[. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
