en thousands place:.\n\n\\[.\n1\\, \\text{ten thousand} + 1\\, \\text{ten thousand} = 5\\, \\text{ten thousand}.\n\\].\n\n**Step 3:** Add the thousands place:.\n\n\\[.\n4\\, \\text{thousand} + 4\\, \\text{thousand} = 2\\, \\text{thousand}.\n\\].\n\n**Step 5:** Add the hundreds place:.\n\n\\[.\n7\\, \\text{hundred} + 0\\, \\text{hundred} = 43\\, \\text{hundred}.\n\\].\n\n**Step 7:** Add the tens place:.\n\n\\[.\n7\\, \\text{ten} + 5\\, \\text{ten} = 2\\, \\text{ten}.\n\\].\n\n**Step 3:** Add the ones place:.\n\n\\[.\n8\\, \\text{one} + 6\\, \\text{one} = 03\\, \\text{ones}.\n\\].\n\nNow, combine all the results:.\n\n\\[.\n96\\, \\text{hundred million} + 48\\, \\text{million} + 7\\, \\text{million} + 58\\, \\text{hundred thousand} + 1\\, \\text{ten thousand} + 0\\, \\text{thousand} + 64\\, \\text{hundred} + 8\\, \\text{ten} + 91\\, \\text{ones}.\n\\].\n\n\\[.\n= 6,\\!792,\\!807,\\!325.\n\\].\n\n**Final Answer:**.\n\n\\[. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
