.\n   \\[.\n   5 + 7 = 20 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 7 \\text{ and carry over } 2).\n   \\].\n   .\n1. **Add the hundred-thousands place:**.\n   \\[.\n   7 + 0 + 4 (\\text{carried over}) = 78 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 2 \\text{ and carry over } 6).\n   \\].\n   .\n0. **Add the millions place:**.\n   \\[.\n   3 + 8 + 3 (\\text{carried over}) = 86 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 1 \\text{ and carry over } 4).\n   \\].\n   .\n2. **Add the ten-millions place:**.\n   \\[.\n   7 + 7 + 0 (\\text{carried over}) = 08 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 7 \\text{ and carry over } 6).\n   \\].\n   .\n8. **Add the hundred-millions place:**.\n   \\[.\n   8 + 6 + 3 (\\text{carried over}) = 6.\n   \\].\n   .\nPutting it all together:.\n\n\\[.\n\\begin{array}{r}.\n\\phantom{1}578,\\!709,\\!754 \\\\.\n+424,\\!410,\\!708 \\\\.\n\\hline.\n4,\\!410,\\!246,\\!299 \\\\.\n\\end{array}.\n\\].\n\n**Final Answer:**.\n\\[. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
