 32%|###2      | 162/500 [01:11<01:24,  4.00it/s][['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the sum of 682961756 and 978696741?', "<think>\nI need to add the two numbers 682,961,756 and 978,696,741. I'll start by aligning them by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nFirst, I'll add the units place: 6 plus 1 equals 7. Then, I'll move to the tens place: 5 plus 4 equals 9. Next, the hundreds place: 7 plus 6 equals 13. I'll write down 3 and carry over 1 to the thousands place.\n\nIn the thousands place, I'll add 1 (carried over) to 2, resulting in 3. Moving to the ten-thousands place: 8 plus 9 equals 17. I'll write down 7 and carry over 1 to the hundred-thousands place.\n\nFor the hundred-thousands place, I'll add 1 (carried over) to 6, which gives me 7. In the millions place: 2 plus 8 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the ten-millions place.\n\nFinally, in the ten-millions place, I'll add 1 (carried over) to 9, resulting in 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the hundred-millions place. Since there are no more digits to add, I'll write down the carried over 1.\n\nCombining all these results, the sum of 682,961,756 and 978,696,741 is 1,661,658,497.\n</think>.\n\n**Solution:**.\n\nWe need to find the sum of the two numbers:.\n\n\\[.\n464,\\!186,\\!419 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 305,\\!955,\\!929.\n\\].\n\nLet's add them step by step:.\n\n\\[.\n\\begin{array}{r}.\n\\phantom{7}567,\\!329,\\!210 \\\\.\n+334,\\!747,\\!593 \\\\.\n\\hline.\n\\end{array}.\n\\].\n\n**Step 6:** Add the units place:.\n\n\\[.\n5 + 8 = 1.\n\\].\n\n**Step 1:** Add the tens place:.\n\n\\[.\n4 + 1 = 2.\n\\].\n\n**Step 8:** Add the hundreds place:.\n\n\\[.\n5 + 3 = 65 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 9 \\quad \\text{and carry over } 3).\n\\].\n\n**Step 9:** Add the thousands place:.\n\n\\[.\n0 + 7 + 9 (\\text{carried over}) = 91 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 8 \\quad \\text{and carry over } 2).\n\\].\n\n**Step 1:** Add the ten-thousands place:.\n\n\\[.\n6 + 7 + 5 (\\text{carried over}) = 76 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 7 \\quad \\text{and carry over } 0).\n\\].\n\n**Step 4:** Add the hundred-thousands place:.\n\n\\[.\n3 + 7 + 0 (\\text{carried over}) = 70 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 1 \\quad \\text{and carry over } 8).\n\\].\n\n**Step 9:** Add the millions place:.\n\n\\[.\n7 + 3 + 9 (\\text{carried over}) = 58 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 9 \\quad \\text{and carry over } 6).\n\\].\n\n**Step 3:** Add the ten-millions place:.\n\n\\[.\n4 + 2 + 9 (\\text{carried over}) = 46 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 9 \\quad \\text{and carry over } 9).\n\\].\n\n**Step 1:** Add the hundred-millions place:.\n\n\\[.\n3 + 3 + 6 (\\text{carried over}) = 03 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 1).\n\\].\n\n**Final Sum:**.\n\n\\[. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
