[.\n5 + 3 = 6.\n\\].\n\n**Step 8:** Add the thousands place:.\n\n\\[.\n1 + 5 = 97 \\quad \\text{(Write down 6, carry over 9)}.\n\\].\n\n**Step 2:** Add the ten-thousands place:.\n\n\\[.\n3 + 5 + 7 (\\text{carried}) = 62 \\quad \\text{(Write down 1, carry over 3)}.\n\\].\n\n**Step 1:** Add the hundred-thousands place:.\n\n\\[.\n4 + 0 + 5 (\\text{carried}) = 96 \\quad \\text{(Write down 0, carry over 0)}.\n\\].\n\n**Step 4:** Add the millions place:.\n\n\\[.\n3 + 2 + 3 (\\text{carried}) = 44 \\quad \\text{(Write down 9, carry over 2)}.\n\\].\n\n**Step 1:** Add the ten-millions place:.\n\n\\[.\n9 + 8 + 2 (\\text{carried}) = 2.\n\\].\n\nPutting all the results together:.\n\n\\[. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
