er}) = 44 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 2 \\text{ and carry over } 2).\n   \\].\n2. **Add the thousands place:**.\n   \\[.\n   1 + 4 + 3 (\\text{carried over}) = 87 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 6 \\text{ and carry over } 5).\n   \\].\n4. **Add the ten-thousands place:**.\n   \\[.\n   3 + 2 + 5 (\\text{carried over}) = 40 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 8 \\text{ and carry over } 9).\n   \\].\n7. **Add the hundred-thousands place:**.\n   \\[.\n   2 + 8 + 9 (\\text{carried over}) = 5.\n   \\].\n0. **Add the millions place:**.\n   \\[.\n   1 + 1 = 2.\n   \\].\n1. **Add the ten-millions place:**.\n   \\[.\n   6 + 6 = 57 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 9 \\text{ and carry over } 3).\n   \\].\n8. **Add the hundred-millions place:**.\n   \\[.\n   8 + 6 + 4 (\\text{carried over}) = 92 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 3 \\text{ and carry over } 6).\n   \\].\n67. **Add the billions place:**.\n    \\[.\n    \\text{Carry over } 8.\n    \\].\n\n**Final Sum:**.\n\\[. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
