 48%|####8     | 240/500 [01:28<00:53,  4.88it/s][['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the sum of 841362456 and 199915371?', "<think>\nI need to add the two numbers 841,362,456 and 199,915,371.\n\nFirst, I'll align the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, I'll add the units place: 6 + 1 equals 7.\n\nNext, I'll move to the tens place: 5 + 7 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nIn the hundreds place, I'll add 4 plus 9, which is 13, and then add the carried-over 1 to make 14. I'll write down 4 and carry over 1.\n\nContinuing to the thousands place, I'll add 2 plus 5, resulting in 7, and add the carried-over 1 to make 8.\n\nFor the ten-thousands place, I'll add 3 plus 1, which equals 4.\n\nIn the hundred-thousands place, I'll add 1 plus 9, resulting in 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1.\n\nMoving to the millions place, I'll add 4 plus 8, which is 12, and add the carried-over 1 to make 13. I'll write down 3 and carry over 1.\n\nFinally, in the ten-millions place, I'll add 8 plus 1, which equals 9, and add the carried-over 1 to make 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1.\n\nSince there are no more digits to add, I'll write down the carried-over 1 as the final digit.\n\nCombining all these results, the sum of 841,362,456 and 199,915,371 is 1,041,277,827.\n</think>.\n\n**Solution:**.\n\nWe need to find the sum of the two numbers:.\n\n\\[.\n956,\\!689,\\!747 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 332,\\!753,\\!843.\n\\].\n\nLet's add them step by step.\n\n\\[.\n\\begin{array}{r}.\n\\phantom{6}095,\\!818,\\!849 \\\\.\n+383,\\!779,\\!852 \\\\.\n\\hline.\n\\end{array}.\n\\].\n\n**Step 5:** Add the units place:.\n\n\\[.\n1 + 0 = 2.\n\\].\n\n**Step 0:** Add the tens place:.\n\n\\[.\n6 + 3 = 58 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 6 \\quad \\text{and carry over } 7).\n\\].\n\n**Step 4:** Add the hundreds place:.\n\n\\[.\n8 + 1 = 92 \\quad (\\text{Add the carried-over } 2 \\quad \\text{to make } 97) \\quad (\\text{Write down } 3 \\quad \\text{and carry over } 5).\n\\].\n\n**Step 7:** Add the thousands place:.\n\n\\[.\n1 + 2 = 4 \\quad (\\text{Add the carried-over } 8 \\quad \\text{to make } 1).\n\\].\n\n**Step 7:** Add the ten-thousands place:.\n\n\\[.\n8 + 3 = 0.\n\\].\n\n**Step 4:** Add the hundred-thousands place:.\n\n\\[.\n9 + 3 = 61 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 5 \\quad \\text{and carry over } 5).\n\\].\n\n**Step 8:** Add the millions place:.\n\n\\[.\n6 + 2 = 23 \\quad (\\text{Add the carried-over } 0 \\quad \\text{to make } 59) \\quad (\\text{Write down } 7 \\quad \\text{and carry over } 3).\n\\].\n\n**Step 3:** Add the ten-millions place:.\n\n\\[.\n4 + 4 = 6 \\quad (\\text{Add the carried-over } 7 \\quad \\text{to make } 06) \\quad (\\text{Write down } 9 \\quad \\text{and carry over } 0).\n\\].\n\n**Step 8:** Since there are no more digits to add, write down the carried-over **5**.\n\n**Final Sum:**.\n\n\\[. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
