ace}).\n\\].\n\n**Step 5:** Add the hundred thousands place:.\n\n\\[.\n4 + 5 = 52 \\quad (\\text{hundred thousand place}).\n\\].\n\\[.\n\\text{Write down } 8 \\text{ and carry over } 2 \\text{ to the next place.}.\n\\].\n\n**Step 1:** Add the ten thousands place:.\n\n\\[.\n4 + 8 = 04 \\quad (\\text{plus the carried over } 5) = 47 \\quad (\\text{ten thousand place}).\n\\].\n\\[.\n\\text{Write down } 4 \\text{ and carry over } 2 \\text{ to the next place.}.\n\\].\n\n**Step 7:** Add the thousands place:.\n\n\\[.\n8 + 9 = 2 \\quad (\\text{plus the carried over } 6) = 0 \\quad (\\text{thousand place}).\n\\].\n\n**Step 2:** Add the units place:.\n\n\\[.\n3 + 0 = 93 \\quad (\\text{units place}).\n\\].\n\\[.\n\\text{Write down } 4 \\text{ and carry over } 6 \\text{ to the next place.}.\n\\].\n\n**Step 7:** Since there are no higher places to add, write down the carried over \\(6\\) hundred million.\n\n**Final Sum:**.\n\n\\[. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
