messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the sum of 667689171 and 440635608?', "<think>\nI need to add the two numbers 667,689,171 and 440,635,608. I'll start by aligning them by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nFirst, I'll add the units place: 1 + 8 equals 9.\n\nNext, I'll move to the tens place: 7 + 0 equals 7.\n\nThen, the hundreds place: 1 + 6 equals 7.\n\nFor the thousands place: 9 + 5 equals 14. I'll write down 4 and carry over 1 to the next place.\n\nIn the ten-thousands place: 8 + 3 plus the carried-over 1 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1.\n\nMoving to the hundred-thousands place: 6 + 6 plus the carried-over 1 equals 13. I'll write down 3 and carry over 1.\n\nIn the millions place: 7 + 4 plus the carried-over 1 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1.\n\nFinally, in the ten-millions place: 6 + 4 plus the carried-over 1 equals 11. I'll write down 11.\n\nCombining all these results, the sum of 667,689,171 and 440,635,608 is 1,108,324,779.\n</think>.\n\n**Solution:**.\n\nWe need to find the sum of the two numbers:.\n\n\\[.\n324,\\!907,\\!717 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 075,\\!116,\\!136.\n\\].\n\nLet's add them step by step:.\n\n\\[.\n\\begin{array}{r}.\n\\phantom{4}881,\\!170,\\!795 \\\\.\n+314,\\!003,\\!417 \\\\.\n\\hline.\n\\end{array}.\n\\].\n\n**Step 8:** Add the units place:.\n\n\\[.\n6 + 9 = 5.\n\\].\n\n**Step 5:** Add the tens place:.\n\n\\[.\n9 + 4 = 5.\n\\].\n\n**Step 2:** Add the hundreds place:.\n\n\\[.\n2 + 9 = 6.\n\\].\n\n**Step 1:** Add the thousands place:.\n\n\\[.\n2 + 6 = 22 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 7 \\text{ and carry over } 6).\n\\].\n\n**Step 0:** Add the ten-thousands place:.\n\n\\[.\n1 + 0 + 6 (\\text{carried over}) = 81 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 1 \\text{ and carry over } 5).\n\\].\n\n**Step 9:** Add the hundred-thousands place:.\n\n\\[.\n2 + 3 + 4 (\\text{carried over}) = 76 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 0 \\text{ and carry over } 2).\n\\].\n\n**Step 6:** Add the millions place:.\n\n\\[.\n9 + 9 + 5 (\\text{carried over}) = 26 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 8 \\text{ and carry over } 9).\n\\].\n\n**Step 3:** Add the ten-millions place:.\n\n\\[.\n1 + 2 + 8 (\\text{carried over}) = 40 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 99).\n\\].\n\n**Final Sum:**.\n\n\\[. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
